  "evidence": "Original N/E/U shows a large, sustained negative excursion in E and U starting near index 552 (P3 onset), with E dropping ~14.7 mm and U ~9.6 mm, persisting through index 582. This is not reversed within the interval; no opposing return is observed. P1 (533–550) shows a small U jump (+2.26 mm) but no matching E/N shift or return; interior points show smooth motion, not a platform. P2 (547–560) overlaps P1/P3 and has inconsistent offsets (E: +0.11, N: -1.05, U: +0.19) — not coherent with either adjacent segment. The only persistent offset is P3’s large step at ~552, but without a return it is a permanent step, not a temporary platform. No genuine temporary offset (sustained shift + opposing return) is supported by observations.",
